Use a **sliding window** with a map of each character’s last-seen index. Move `left` forward whenever the current character was seen inside the current window.

```js
function longestUniqueSubstring(s) {
  const lastSeen = new Map();
  let left = 0;
  let bestStart = 0;
  let bestLen = 0;

  for (let right = 0; right < s.length; right++) {
    const ch = s[right];

    if (lastSeen.has(ch) && lastSeen.get(ch) >= left) {
      left = lastSeen.get(ch) + 1;
    }

    lastSeen.set(ch, right);

    const currentLen = right - left + 1;
    if (currentLen > bestLen) {
      bestLen = currentLen;
      bestStart = left;
    }
  }

  return {
    length: bestLen,
    substring: s.slice(bestStart, bestStart + bestLen)
  };
}

console.log(longestUniqueSubstring("abbaacdefb"));
// { length: 6, substring: "acdefb" }
```

Trace for `"abbaacdefb"`:

| right | char | action | left | current window | best so far |
|---:|---|---|---:|---|---|
| 0 | a | add a | 0 | `a` | `a` length 1 |
| 1 | b | add b | 0 | `ab` | `ab` length 2 |
| 2 | b | b repeated, move left to 2 | 2 | `b` | `ab` length 2 |
| 3 | a | a last seen before left, no move | 2 | `ba` | `ab` length 2 |
| 4 | a | a repeated, move left to 4 | 4 | `a` | `ab` length 2 |
| 5 | c | add c | 4 | `ac` | `ab` length 2 |
| 6 | d | add d | 4 | `acd` | `acd` length 3 |
| 7 | e | add e | 4 | `acde` | `acde` length 4 |
| 8 | f | add f | 4 | `acdef` | `acdef` length 5 |
| 9 | b | b last seen before left, no move | 4 | `acdefb` | `acdefb` length 6 |

So the longest substring without repeated characters is:

```js
"acdefb"
```

with length `6`.

Time complexity: `O(n)`  
Space complexity: `O(k)`, where `k` is the number of unique characters.

